  "description": "EMIBAG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H80 Dy4 N4 O24,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.376-3.711 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.55-103.22°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(L1)2(L2)4(NO3)2(EtOH)4]·2MeOH (C84H88Dy4N4O26). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
